+/*
+ * SPDX-License-Identifier: APSL-2.0
+ *
+ * NEGRONI (OnePlus 10 Pro 5G NE2211, SM8450): GNSS through the modem, patch 0397 of iOSPlus10
+ * (docs/location-plan.md path L3/C, patches/xnu/README-gnss.md). UNTESTED ON HARDWARE.
+ *
+ * The NE2211 has no GNSS chip of its own: the GNSS engine is in the modem (MPSS, a Hexagon DSP), and the
+ * modem speaks QMI LOC (service 16) over QRTR. This file starts the modem in its default (low power,
+ * never "online") mode, serves the three things the modem asks the HLOS for before it offers its
+ * services (RMTFS, TFTP, the service registry locator), and runs a QMI LOC client. Fixes go to
+ * /dev/negroni_gnss and sysctl kern.negroni_gnss (text, format below) for userland/location/negroni-locd.
+ *
+ * Feature rules (CLAUDE.md "No probes"): on by default; boot-arg negronignss=0 is the only switch (kill
+ * switch). The steps below are the self-check. Any failure stops and powers the modem down (if it was
+ * started), and prints ONE line "NEGRONI GNSS: off: <reason>". A modem crash (SMP2P FATAL), a dead GLINK
+ * or a modem that stops answering after "on" does the same. No restart in that boot.
+ *
+ * Sources. Linux qcom_q6v5_pas.c sm8450_mpss_resource (pas_id 4, crash reason 421, load_state "modem",
+ * proxy power domains cx + mss); the live DT (out/live.dts): remoteproc-mss@04080000, mpss_region@8bc00000
+ * size 0x13200000, qcom,smp2p-modem (items in 435 / out 428, remote pid 1, IPCC client 2 signal 2),
+ * glink-edge "mpss" (IPCC client 2 signal 0, channel IPCRTR), qcom,rmtfs_sharedmem@0 (0x280000, client 1,
+ * no qcom,vm-nav-path). The PAS/SMEM/SMP2P/GLINK/QRTR code is negroni_slpi.c (0376, itself a copy of the
+ * ADSP code 0240/0242/0248) with the modem's numbers. The RMTFS, TFTP and service-registry servers and the
+ * QRTR name service are ported from HakiOS xnu/files/bsd/dev/hakios.mpss.c (APSL 2.0, Copyright (c)
+ * 2025-2026 the HakiOS authors; reference tree out/src/hackios-next, commit
+ * 88513176b1e96ecf0b764cd62c6f4e6ac71345e3), whose modem runs on SM7325 with the same protocol. QMI LOC
+ * and DMS message and TLV numbers: libqmi data/qmi-service-loc.json, qmi-service-dms.json,
+ * qmi-flags64-loc.h, qmi-enums-loc.h (gitlab.freedesktop.org/mobile-broadband/libqmi
+ * 3454c2c619d516fd46a08fe16c6eebdee061857d).
+ *
+ * Steps (thread "NEGRONI GNSS", after GN_SETTLE_S seconds of boot):
+ *   0  waits   for the ADSP (0240) and SLPI (0376) start threads if they run (QMP mailbox, TCSR mutex 3)
+ *   1  reads   SMEM: the apps<->modem partition (hosts 0/1); the modem's SMP2P item 435 must be absent
+ *   2  reads   UFS LUN 4 "modem_a" (FAT16, READ ONLY): image/modem.mdt + modem.bNN, the image/NAME.jsn files
+ *   3  reads   UFS LUN 5 modemst1, modemst2, fsg, fsc (READ ONLY) into kernel memory: the RMTFS backing.
+ *              The modem's writes go into that memory only. Nothing in this file can write a partition.
+ *   4  maps    the RMTFS buffer (GN_RMTFS_PHYS: below 4 GiB, outside XNU's RAM), zero, pattern check
+ *   5  writes  RPMh: mss.lvl level 384 (the modem's own rail; never cx.lvl, which USB and UFS share)
+ *   6  writes  AOSS QMP: "{class: image, res: load_state, name: modem, val: on}"
+ *   7  asks    TrustZone: PAS init image (id 4), PAS mem setup (0x8bc00000, span)
+ *   8  writes  the carveout 0x8bc00000 + 0x13200000 only: zero, PT_LOAD segments, read back (SHA-256)
+ *   9  writes  SMEM: our SMP2P item 428 ("master-kernel" = 0), IPCC ring (client 2, signal 2)
+ *  10  asks    TrustZone: SCM memory assign of the RMTFS buffer to HLOS + MSS_MSA (the DT has no NAV path),
+ *              PAS auth and reset (id 4); waits for "slave-kernel" READY (handover drops the mss vote)
+ *  11  writes  SMEM: GLINK items 478 + 479 (0/1 partition); version; channel IPCRTR
+ *  12  talks   QRTR: HELLO; serves RMTFS (14), TFTP (4096), servreg locator (64); waits for LOC (16)
+ *  13  talks   QMI LOC: register events (answer OK = the last self-check), engine lock none, standalone
+ * Then "NEGRONI GNSS: on: ..." and the run loop: GLINK polled every 200 ms (50 ms with a session), the
+ * modem's SMP2P FATAL bit watched (0248 style), a LOC request every 30 s as a liveness check (3 lost answers
+ * = off). A LOC session (periodic, 1 s) runs while /dev/negroni_gnss was read in the last GN_DEMAND_S
+ * seconds; without readers it stops (GNSS off, modem idle).
+ *
+ * USB safety (README-gnss.md "USB"): the USB drop after the ADSP start (notes 48/55/58) comes from the ADSP
+ * charger PD (Type-C role flip, PHY rails). The modem owns no USB, Type-C, PMIC or PHY resource; this file
+ * writes no GPIO, clock, PMIC or USB register, and votes only mss.lvl (modem-only). UFS: only READ(10) on
+ * other LUNs, one 1 MiB command at a time under the UFS lock (root I/O interleaves).
+ *
+ * Interface (docs/location-plan.md section 6): /dev/negroni_gnss root:wheel 0440, pread(fd, buf, n, 0) gives
+ *   state=<starting|on|off> session=<0|1> engine=<on|off|unknown> reports=<N> reason=<text>\n
+ *   fix=<seq> final=<0|1> utc_ms=<ms> lat=<deg> lon=<deg> alt_m=<m|-> ealt_m=<m|-> hacc_m=<m|-> vacc_m=<m|->
+ *       speed_mps=<m/s|-> course_deg=<deg|-> sats=<n> age_ms=<ms>\n      (second line only after a fix)
+ *   locd=LAT LON HACC ALT VACC SPEED COURSE\n   (third line only for a fix younger than 3 s; negroni-locd's text form)
+ * Each device read counts as demand; kern.negroni_gnss gives the same text and is not demand.
+ */
